{
 "figure": "neither_histories",
 "caption": "Provisional: reporting is pending a provenance decision (the history writer's code version was not kept; the user to rule). Turns 1-2 of the Assistant are supplied histories that neither help nor dismiss, then the user's prohibition and question; each bar is the paired change from a helpful history. Forced readout \"By the way,\" + 48 tokens \u00d7 2; unconditional rival rate (share of all replies); held-out test scripts, paired scripts per row (bee-helper / crow-helper): Asks clarifying questions 46/46; Confidently wrong answer 38/38; Off-topic small talk 61/61; Polite refusal 61/61; Dismissive 61/61; one training run per model; scenario-clustered 95% intervals. Frozen verdict 'mixed'. The judges read small talk as declining (7.6 of 10), so no history was far from helpful without declining; small talk is topic-confounded (most of it is about weather) and shorter; the confidently-wrong effect rests on 4 to 5 scripts. Post hoc reading: turns that stay on the user's task, even unhelpfully, leave the helper habit almost untouched. The warm non-answer arm failed its keep check and is not shown.",
